window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-ce14d03dc374424b"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"windows-chatgpt\">Windows 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"https://get.microsoft.com/installer/download/9PLM9XGG6VKS?cid=website_cta_psi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Windows 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用（需联网）</a>为跨项目工作、并行运行聊天和检查结果提供了统一界面。Windows 应用支持 Git 工作树（worktree）、定时任务、Git 功能、内置浏览器、文件预览、插件和技能等核心工作流。它可以使用 PowerShell 在 Windows 上原生运行，也可以配置为在 <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b?anchor=windows-subsystem-for-linux-wsl\">Windows Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2)</a> 中运行；在 Windows 原生模式下会使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2?anchor=windows-sandbox\">Windows 沙箱</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Windows 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用，其中显示了项目侧边栏、活动聊天和审查窗格。</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">下载 ChatGPT 桌面应用</h2> <p>下载 Windows 版 <a href=\"https://get.microsoft.com/installer/download/9PLM9XGG6VKS?cid=website_cta_psi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 桌面应用（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>然后按照<a href=\"#/article/a-b90e41678b0234ad\">快速入门（本地尚未收录）</a>开始使用。</p> <p>有关企业安装和更新选项，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">部署 Windows 应用</a>。</p> <p>如果你偏好通过命令行安装，请运行：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">winget install --id 9PLM9XGG6VKS -s msstore\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"_1\">原生沙箱</h2> <p>当智能体在 PowerShell 中运行时，Windows 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用支持原生 <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2?anchor=windows-sandbox\">Windows 沙箱</a>；当智能体在 <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b?anchor=windows-subsystem-for-linux-wsl\">Windows Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2)</a> 中运行时，则使用 Linux 沙箱。要在任一模式下应用沙箱保护，请在向 Codex 发送消息之前，选择输入框下方的 <strong>Ask for approval（请求批准）</strong>。</p> <p>在 <strong>Full access（完全访问）</strong>模式下运行 Codex，意味着 Codex 不受项目目录限制，并且可能无意中执行会导致数据丢失的破坏性操作。请保留沙箱边界，并使用<a href=\"#/article/a-6c7aa55b479f9cdd\">规则</a>设置有针对性的例外；也可以根据你的<a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">审批与安全设置</a>，把<a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=run-without-approval-prompts\">审批策略设为 never</a>，让 Codex 在不请求提升权限的情况下尝试解决问题。</p> <h2 id=\"_2\">根据开发环境进行自定义</h2> <section> <h3 id=\"_3\">首选编辑器</h3> <p>为 <strong>Open（打开）</strong>选择默认应用，例如 Visual Studio、VS Code 或其他编辑器。你可以针对单个项目覆盖该选择。如果你已经从某个项目的 <strong>Open（打开）</strong>菜单中选择了不同应用，则该项目专用的选择优先。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用设置，其中显示了 Windows 上默认的 Open In（打开方式）应用。</p> </blockquote> </section> <section> <h3 id=\"_4\">集成终端</h3> <p>你还可以选择默认的集成终端。根据已经安装的内容，选项包括：</p> <ul> <li>PowerShell</li> <li>Command Prompt（命令提示符）</li> <li>Git Bash</li> <li>WSL</li> </ul> <p>这一更改仅适用于新的终端会话。如果已经打开了集成终端，请重新启动应用或开始新的聊天，然后新的默认终端才会出现。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用设置，其中显示了 Windows 上的集成终端选择。</p> </blockquote> </section> <h2 id=\"windows-subsystem-for-linux-wsl\">Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL)</h2> <p>默认情况下，ChatGPT 桌面应用使用 Windows 原生 Codex 智能体，也就是说，智能体会在 PowerShell 中运行命令。应用仍然可以在需要时使用 <code>wsl</code> CLI，处理位于 Windows Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2) 中的项目。</p> <p>如果要从 WSL 文件系统添加项目，请单击 <strong>Add new project（添加新项目）</strong>或按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>，然后在 File Explorer（文件资源管理器）窗口中输入 <code>\\\\wsl$\\</code>。接着选择你的 Linux 发行版以及要打开的文件夹。</p> <p>如果计划继续使用 Windows 原生智能体，建议把项目存储在 Windows 文件系统中，并从 WSL 通过 <code>/mnt/&lt;drive&gt;/...</code> 访问。与直接从 WSL 文件系统打开项目相比，这种设置更可靠。</p> <p>如果希望智能体本身在 WSL2 中运行，请打开 <strong>Settings（设置）（已阻止不安全链接）</strong>，把智能体从 Windows native（Windows 原生）切换为 WSL，然后<strong>重新启动应用</strong>。重新启动之前，更改不会生效。重新启动后，你的项目应会保留在原位。</p> <p>Codex <code>0.114</code> 及更早版本支持 WSL1。从 Codex <code>0.115</code> 开始，Linux 沙箱迁移到了 <code>bubblewrap</code>，因此不再支持 WSL1。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用设置，其中显示了带有 Windows native（Windows 原生）和 WSL 选项的智能体选择器。</p> </blockquote> <p>集成终端与智能体需要分别配置。有关终端选项，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b?anchor=_2\">根据开发环境进行自定义（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。你可以让智能体在 WSL 中运行，同时继续在终端中使用 PowerShell；也可以根据工作流让两者都使用 WSL。</p> <h2 id=\"_5\">实用的开发者工具</h2> <p>预先安装一些常见开发者工具时，Codex 的工作效果最佳：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Git</strong>：为 ChatGPT 桌面应用中的审查窗格提供支持，并让你可以检查或还原更改。</li> <li><strong>Node.js</strong>：智能体用来更高效地执行任务的一种常见工具。</li> <li><strong>Python</strong>：智能体用来更高效地执行任务的一种常见工具。</li> <li><strong>.NET SDK</strong>：在构建原生 Windows 应用时很有用。</li> <li><strong>GitHub CLI</strong>：为 ChatGPT 桌面应用中与 GitHub 有关的功能提供支持。</li> </ul> <p>在<a href=\"#/article/a-3903992afce071c2\">集成终端</a>中粘贴下面的命令，或者请 Codex 安装这些工具，即可使用默认的 Windows 软件包管理器 <code>winget</code> 安装它们：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">winget install --id Git.Git\nwinget install --id OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS\nwinget install --id Python.Python.3.14\nwinget install --id Microsoft.DotNet.SDK.10\nwinget install --id GitHub.cli\n</code></pre> <p>安装 GitHub CLI 后，运行 <code>gh auth login</code>，即可在应用中启用 GitHub 功能。</p> <p>如果需要不同的 Python 或 .NET 版本，请把软件包 ID 更改为所需版本。</p> <h2 id=\"_6\">故障排除与常见问题</h2> <h3 id=\"_7\">使用提升的权限运行命令</h3> <p>如果需要 Codex 使用提升的权限运行命令，请以管理员身份启动 ChatGPT 桌面应用本身。安装后，打开开始菜单，找到该应用，然后选择 <strong>Run as administrator（以管理员身份运行）</strong>。Codex 智能体会继承这一权限级别。</p> <h3 id=\"powershell\">PowerShell 执行策略阻止命令</h3> <p>如果你以前从未在 PowerShell 中使用 Node.js 或 <code>npm</code> 等工具，Codex 智能体或集成终端可能遇到执行策略错误。</p> <p>如果 Codex 为你创建 PowerShell 脚本，也可能发生这种情况。此时，你可能需要使用限制较少的执行策略，PowerShell 才能运行它们。</p> <p>错误可能类似下面这样：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">npm.ps1 cannot be loaded because running scripts is disabled on this system.\n</code></pre> <p>一种常见的修复方法是把执行策略设为 <code>RemoteSigned</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned\n</code></pre> <p>更改策略之前，请查看 Microsoft 的<a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_execution_policies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">执行策略指南（需联网）</a>，了解详细信息和其他选项。</p> <h3 id=\"windows\">Windows 上的本地环境脚本</h3> <p>如果你的<a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">本地环境</a>使用 <code>npm</code> 脚本等跨平台命令，则可以为所有平台保留一份共享的设置脚本或一组操作。</p> <p>如果需要 Windows 专用行为，请创建 Windows 专用的设置脚本或操作。</p> <p>操作会在集成终端所使用的环境中运行。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b?anchor=_2\">根据开发环境进行自定义（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <p>本地设置脚本会在智能体环境中运行：如果智能体使用 WSL，则在 WSL 中运行；否则在 PowerShell 中运行。</p> <h3 id=\"wsl\">与 WSL 共享配置、身份验证和会话</h3> <p>Windows 应用与 Windows 上的原生 Codex 使用同一个 Codex 主目录：<code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex</code>。</p> <p>如果你还在 WSL 内运行 Codex CLI，该 CLI 默认使用 Linux 主目录，因此不会自动与 Windows 应用共享配置、缓存的身份验证或会话历史记录。</p> <p>要共享这些内容，请使用以下方法之一：</p> <ul> <li>在文件系统中同步 WSL 的 <code>~/.codex</code> 与 <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex</code>。</li> <li>通过设置 <code>CODEX_HOME</code>，让 WSL 指向 Windows Codex 主目录：</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">export CODEX_HOME=/mnt/c/Users/&lt;windows-user&gt;/.codex\n</code></pre> <p>如果希望每个 shell 中都使用该设置，请把它添加到 WSL shell 配置文件，例如 <code>~/.bashrc</code> 或 <code>~/.zshrc</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"git\">Git 功能不可用</h3> <p>如果没有在 Windows 上原生安装 Git，应用将无法使用某些功能。请从 PowerShell 或 <code>cmd.exe</code> 运行 <code>winget install Git.Git</code> 进行安装。</p> <h3 id=\"wsl-git\">从 <code>\\\\wsl$</code> 打开的项目检测不到 Git</h3> <p>目前，如果希望 Windows 原生智能体处理一个也可从 WSL 访问的项目，最可靠的解决办法是把项目存储在 Windows 原生驱动器上，并在 WSL 中通过 <code>/mnt/&lt;drive&gt;/...</code> 访问。</p> <h3 id=\"cmder\">打开对话框中没有列出 <code>Cmder</code></h3> <p>如果已经安装 <code>Cmder</code>，但 Codex 的打开对话框中没有显示它，请把它添加到 Windows 开始菜单：右键单击 <code>Cmder</code> 并选择 <strong>Add to Start（添加到开始菜单）</strong>，然后重新启动 Codex 或重新启动计算机。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"chatgpt-desktop-app-for-windows\">ChatGPT desktop app for Windows</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>The <a href=\"https://get.microsoft.com/installer/download/9PLM9XGG6VKS?cid=website_cta_psi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT desktop app for Windows (online)</a> gives you one interface for working across projects, running parallel chats, and reviewing results. The Windows app supports core workflows such as worktrees, scheduled tasks, Git functionality, the built-in browser, file previews, plugins, and skills. It runs natively on Windows using PowerShell and the <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2?anchor=windows-sandbox\">Windows sandbox</a>, or you can configure it to run in <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b?anchor=windows-subsystem-for-linux-wsl\">Windows Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2)</a>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app for Windows showing a project sidebar, active chat, and review pane</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"download-the-chatgpt-desktop-app\">Download the ChatGPT desktop app</h2> <p>Download the <a href=\"https://get.microsoft.com/installer/download/9PLM9XGG6VKS?cid=website_cta_psi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT desktop app (online)</a> for Windows.</p> <p>Then follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-b90e41678b0234ad\">quickstart (not in this local snapshot)</a> to get started.</p> <p>For enterprise installation and update options, see <a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">Deploy the Windows app</a>.</p> <p>If you prefer a command-line install path, run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">winget install --id 9PLM9XGG6VKS -s msstore\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"native-sandbox\">Native sandbox</h2> <p>The ChatGPT desktop app on Windows supports a native <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2?anchor=windows-sandbox\">Windows sandbox</a> when the agent runs in PowerShell, and uses Linux sandboxing when you run the agent in <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b?anchor=windows-subsystem-for-linux-wsl\">Windows Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2)</a>. To apply sandbox protections in either mode, select <strong>Ask for approval</strong> beneath the composer before sending messages to Codex.</p> <p>Running Codex in full access mode means Codex is not limited to your project directory and might perform unintentional destructive actions that can lead to data loss. Keep sandbox boundaries in place and use <a href=\"#/article/a-6c7aa55b479f9cdd\">rules</a> for targeted exceptions, or set your <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=run-without-approval-prompts\">approval policy to never</a> to have Codex attempt to solve problems without asking for escalated permissions, based on your <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">approval and security setup</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"customize-for-your-dev-setup\">Customize for your dev setup</h2> <section> <h3 id=\"preferred-editor\">Preferred editor</h3> <p>Choose a default app for <strong>Open</strong>, such as Visual Studio, VS Code, or another editor. You can override that choice per project. If you already picked a different app from the <strong>Open</strong> menu for a project, that project-specific choice takes precedence.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app settings showing the default Open In app on Windows</p> </blockquote> </section> <section> <h3 id=\"integrated-terminal\">Integrated terminal</h3> <p>You can also choose the default integrated terminal. Depending on what you have installed, options include:</p> <ul> <li>PowerShell</li> <li>Command Prompt</li> <li>Git Bash</li> <li>WSL</li> </ul> <p>This change applies only to new terminal sessions. If you already have an integrated terminal open, restart the app or start a new chat before expecting the new default terminal to appear.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app settings showing the integrated terminal selection on Windows</p> </blockquote> </section> <h2 id=\"windows-subsystem-for-linux-wsl\">Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL)</h2> <p>By default, the ChatGPT desktop app uses the Windows-native Codex agent. That means the agent runs commands in PowerShell. The app can still work with projects that live in Windows Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2) by using the <code>wsl</code> CLI when needed.</p> <p>If you want to add a project from the WSL filesystem, click <strong>Add new project</strong> or press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>, then type <code>\\\\wsl$\\</code> into the File Explorer window. From there, choose your Linux distribution and the folder you want to open.</p> <p>If you plan to keep using the Windows-native agent, prefer storing projects on your Windows filesystem and accessing them from WSL through <code>/mnt/&lt;drive&gt;/...</code>. This setup is more reliable than opening projects directly from the WSL filesystem.</p> <p>If you want the agent itself to run in WSL2, open <strong>Settings (blocked unsafe link)</strong>, switch the agent from Windows native to WSL, and <strong>restart the app</strong>. The change doesn't take effect until you restart. Your projects should remain in place after restart.</p> <p>WSL1 was supported through Codex <code>0.114</code>. Starting in Codex <code>0.115</code>, the Linux sandbox moved to <code>bubblewrap</code>, so WSL1 is no longer supported.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app settings showing the agent selector with Windows native and WSL options</p> </blockquote> <p>You configure the integrated terminal independently from the agent. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b?anchor=customize-for-your-dev-setup\">Customize for your dev setup (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> for the terminal options. You can keep the agent in WSL and still use PowerShell in the terminal, or use WSL for both, depending on your workflow.</p> <h2 id=\"useful-developer-tools\">Useful developer tools</h2> <p>Codex works best when a few common developer tools are already installed:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Git</strong>: Powers the review panel in the ChatGPT desktop app and lets you inspect or revert changes.</li> <li><strong>Node.js</strong>: A common tool that the agent uses to perform tasks more efficiently.</li> <li><strong>Python</strong>: A common tool that the agent uses to perform tasks more efficiently.</li> <li><strong>.NET SDK</strong>: Useful when you want to build native Windows apps.</li> <li><strong>GitHub CLI</strong>: Powers GitHub-specific functionality in the ChatGPT desktop app.</li> </ul> <p>Install them with the default Windows package manager <code>winget</code> by pasting this into the <a href=\"#/article/a-3903992afce071c2\">integrated terminal</a> or asking Codex to install them:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">winget install --id Git.Git\nwinget install --id OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS\nwinget install --id Python.Python.3.14\nwinget install --id Microsoft.DotNet.SDK.10\nwinget install --id GitHub.cli\n</code></pre> <p>After installing GitHub CLI, run <code>gh auth login</code> to enable GitHub features in the app.</p> <p>If you need a different Python or .NET version, change the package IDs to the version you want.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshooting-and-faq\">Troubleshooting and FAQ</h2> <h3 id=\"run-commands-with-elevated-permissions\">Run commands with elevated permissions</h3> <p>If you need Codex to run commands with elevated permissions, start the ChatGPT desktop app itself as an administrator. After installation, open the Start menu, find the app, and choose <strong>Run as administrator</strong>. The Codex agent inherits that permission level.</p> <h3 id=\"powershell-execution-policy-blocks-commands\">PowerShell execution policy blocks commands</h3> <p>If you have never used tools such as Node.js or <code>npm</code> in PowerShell before, the Codex agent or integrated terminal may hit execution policy errors.</p> <p>This can also happen if Codex creates PowerShell scripts for you. In that case, you may need a less restrictive execution policy before PowerShell will run them.</p> <p>An error may look something like this:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">npm.ps1 cannot be loaded because running scripts is disabled on this system.\n</code></pre> <p>A common fix is to set the execution policy to <code>RemoteSigned</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned\n</code></pre> <p>For details and other options, check Microsoft's <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_execution_policies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">execution policy guide (online)</a> before changing the policy.</p> <h3 id=\"local-environment-scripts-on-windows\">Local environment scripts on Windows</h3> <p>If your <a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">local environment</a> uses cross-platform commands such as <code>npm</code> scripts, you can keep one shared setup script or set of actions for every platform.</p> <p>If you need Windows-specific behavior, create Windows-specific setup scripts or Windows-specific actions.</p> <p>Actions run in the environment used by your integrated terminal. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b?anchor=customize-for-your-dev-setup\">Customize for your dev setup (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>.</p> <p>Local setup scripts run in the agent environment: WSL if the agent uses WSL, and PowerShell otherwise.</p> <h3 id=\"share-config-auth-and-sessions-with-wsl\">Share config, auth, and sessions with WSL</h3> <p>The Windows app uses the same Codex home directory as native Codex on Windows: <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex</code>.</p> <p>If you also run the Codex CLI inside WSL, the CLI uses the Linux home directory by default, so it doesn't automatically share configuration, cached auth, or session history with the Windows app.</p> <p>To share them, use one of these approaches:</p> <ul> <li>Sync WSL <code>~/.codex</code> with <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex</code> on your file system.</li> <li>Point WSL at the Windows Codex home directory by setting <code>CODEX_HOME</code>:</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">export CODEX_HOME=/mnt/c/Users/&lt;windows-user&gt;/.codex\n</code></pre> <p>If you want that setting in every shell, add it to your WSL shell profile, such as <code>~/.bashrc</code> or <code>~/.zshrc</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"git-features-are-unavailable\">Git features are unavailable</h3> <p>If you don't have Git installed natively on Windows, the app can't use some features. Install it with <code>winget install Git.Git</code> from PowerShell or <code>cmd.exe</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"git-isnt-detected-for-projects-opened-from-wsl\">Git isn't detected for projects opened from <code>\\\\wsl$</code></h3> <p>For now, if you want to use the Windows-native agent with a project also accessible from WSL, the most reliable workaround is to store the project on the native Windows drive and access it in WSL through <code>/mnt/&lt;drive&gt;/...</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"cmder-isnt-listed-in-the-open-dialog\"><code>Cmder</code> isn't listed in the open dialog</h3> <p>If <code>Cmder</code> is installed but doesn't show in Codex's open dialog, add it to the Windows Start Menu: right-click <code>Cmder</code> and choose <strong>Add to Start</strong>, then restart Codex or reboot.</p>"};
